# Day 24 - Ransom Note

## Problem Statement
Given two strings `ransomNote` and `magazine`, return `true` if `ransomNote` can be constructed using the letters from `magazine`; otherwise, return `false`.

Each letter in `magazine` can be used at most once.

## Code

class Solution {
public:
    bool canConstruct(string ransomNote, string magazine) {
        if (magazine.length() < ransomNote.length()) {
            return false;
        }

        vector<int> freq(26, 0);

        for (char c : ransomNote) {
            freq[c - 'a']++;
        }

        for (char c : magazine) {
            freq[c - 'a']--;
        }

        for (int i = 0; i < 26; i++) {
            if (freq[i] > 0) {
                return false;
            }
        }

        return true;
    }
};




## Time Complexity
**O(n + m)**

## Space Complexity
**O(1)**

## Approach
This solution uses a **frequency array** of size `26` to count the occurrences of each lowercase English letter. First, the frequency of every character in `ransomNote` is incremented. Then, while traversing `magazine`, the corresponding frequency is decremented for each character found. After processing both strings, if any frequency remains positive, it means that `magazine` does not contain enough occurrences of that character to construct `ransomNote`, so the function returns `false`. Otherwise, all required characters are available, and the function returns `true`.
